<title>JAPAN: Moderate quake jolts central Japan.</title>
<headline>Moderate quake jolts central Japan.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>An earthquake measuring 4.9 on the Richter scale jolted parts of central Japan on Friday and was felt as a mild tremor in Tokyo, but there were no immediate reports of damage or injuries, the Meteorological Agency reported.</p>
<p>The agency said the earthquake came at 12.25 p.m. (0325 GMT) and was centred in Yamanashi prefecture, about 100 km (60 miles) west of Tokyo.</p>
